{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: make a landing fold the workroom once instead of three times.\n\nhugh asked in chat on 2026-10-13 why `gs land` is sometimes very slow in the artroom workroom, and approved filing this.\n\nMeasured on 2026-10-13 against artroom (depth 38,186; 16,684 artifacts; 141 merge receipts) with gs built from 02090dc: one local fold takes 23 to 28 seconds of CPU, and a read-only `gs merge-plan --server` takes 24.6 seconds. Git is not the cost: 13 git processes, `git status` 14 ms.\n\nA landing pays that fold three times. `previewMerge` (cmd/gs/land.go:215@dd81a392) and `mergeLocked` (cmd/gs/main.go:957@dd81a392) each call `mergeplan.Build`, which calls `Workspace.ReadOnlySnapshot` (internal/mergeplan/mergeplan.go:1439@dd81a392). That path is uncached by contract, for diagnostic surfaces that must leave no local acceleration state. Between them `validateMerge` (cmd/gs/main.go:861@dd81a392) calls `Workspace.Snapshot`, which starts cold because the read-only path left no cache. The third fold also opens a window of a whole fold before the frontier check at cmd/gs/main.go:1029@dd81a392, so in a busy room the merge often reports \"workroom frontier moved after planning\" and plans again.\n\n`gs land` and `gs merge` are writing commands, not diagnostic surfaces. Let the plan they build read the workspace's cached snapshot. Keep the read-only path for `gs merge-plan` and the MCP `merge_plan` tool.","body":{"conditions":"1. gs land and gs merge build their merge plan from Workspace.Snapshot, so one landing at an unmoved frontier performs one full fold; a test counts the folds and goes red when either call site returns to the read-only path. 2. gs merge-plan and the MCP merge_plan tool keep ReadOnlySnapshot and still publish no checkpoint and advance no verified-frontier witness; an existing or new test pins this. 3. The plan a landing builds from the cached snapshot equals the plan the read-only path builds at the same frontier; a test compares them. 4. docs/reference/architecture.md states which callers use which path, in the same head. 5. go test ./... passes at the head. 6. The report states the before and after wall time of gs merge-plan and of the land path measured on a copy of the artroom log, or says plainly what was not measured.","target_head":"dd81a3929e89ff81a4fccad9f06a5622e855d4d1","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}